.TH PKCSCCA 1 "August 2026" "@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "openCryptoki"
.SH NAME
pkcscca \- configuration utility for the CCA token

.SH SYNOPSIS
.SS "VERSION MIGRATION"
\fBpkcscca\fP
\fB-m v2objectsv3\fP
[\fB-d\fP \fIdirectory\fP]
[\fB-v\fP \fILEVEL\fP]

.SS "KEY MIGRATION"
\fBpkcscca\fP
\fB-m keys\fP
\fB-s\fP \fISLOTID\fP
\fB-k aes|apka|asym|sym\fP
[\fB-d\fP \fIdirectory\fP]
[\fB-v\fP \fILEVEL\fP]

.SS "OLD RSA KEY MIGRATION"
\fBpkcscca\fP
\fB-m oldrsakeys\fP
\fB-s\fP \fISLOTID\fP
[\fB-d\fP \fIdirectory\fP]
[\fB-v\fP \fILEVEL\fP]

.SS "HELP"
\fBpkcscca\fP \fB-h\fP

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBpkcscca\fP utility assists in administering the CCA token.

In version 2 of opencryptoki, CCA private token objects were encrypted in CCA
hardware. In version 3 these objects are encrypted in software. The
\fBv2objectsv3\fP migration option migrates these v2 objects by
decrypting them in CCA hardware using a secure key and then re-encrypting
them in software using a software key. Afterwards, v2 objects can be accessed
in version 3.

There may be situations where CCA master keys must be changed. All CCA secret
and private keys are wrapped with a master key. After a CCA master key is
changed, keys wrapped with the old master key need to be re-wrapped with the
current master key. The \fBkeys\fP migration option migrates these wrapped keys
by unwrapping them with the old master key and wrapping them with the current
master key.

Up to opencryptoki version 3.14.0, RSA keys were created using the RSA-CRT
key token format (private key section X'08'). RSA-CRT keys are encrypted with
the CCA ASYM master key, and cannot be used for certain mechanisms, e.g.
RSA-PSS or RSA-OAEP. In newer opencryptoki versions, RSA keys are created using
the RSA-AESC key token format (private key section X'31'). Up to version 3.16.0,
RSA public keys also contained full CCA secure key tokens, including the private
key section (which is encrypted by the CCA master key). The \fBoldrsakeys\fP
migration option migrates old RSA private key tokens to the new format, and also
extracts the public key sections from RSA public key tokens containing a full
CCA secure key token.

.SH "GENERAL OPTIONS"
.IP "\fB-h\fP" 5
Print a help message and exit.
.IP "\fB-d\fP|\fB--datastore\fP \fIdirectory\fP" 10
The directory where the CCA token information is kept. This directory will be
used to locate the private token objects to be migrated,
e.g. \fI@localstatedir@/lib/opencryptoki/ccatok\fP.
If not specified, the compiled-in default \fI@localstatedir@/lib/opencryptoki/ccatok\fP is used.
.IP "\fB-v\fP|\fB--verbose\fP \fILEVEL\fP" 5
Set the verbosity level. \fILEVEL\fP must be one of:
.RS
.TP
\fBnone\fP
No extra output (default).
.TP
\fBerror\fP
Report errors only.
.TP
\fBwarn\fP
Report warnings and errors.
.TP
\fBinfo\fP
Report informational messages, warnings, and errors.
.TP
\fBdevel\fP
Report developer-level messages and all of the above.
.TP
\fBdebug\fP
Report all debug messages (most verbose).
.RE

.SH "VERSION MIGRATION"
.IP "\fB-m v2objectsv3\fP" 5
Migrates CCA private token objects from CCA encryption (used in v2) to software
encryption (used in v3).

.SH "KEY MIGRATION"
.IP "\fB-m keys\fP" 5
Unwraps private keys with an old CCA master key and wraps them with a new CCA
master key.
.IP "\fB-k aes|apka|asym|sym\fP" 5
Migrate keys wrapped with the selected CCA master key type.
The argument selects which master key domain to target:
.RS
.TP
\fBaes\fP
AES-DATA keys, AES-CIPHER keys (including AES-XTS), and HMAC keys
(all wrapped with the CCA AES master key).
.TP
\fBapka\fP
New-format RSA keys (RSA-AESC / RSA-AESM), ECC keys, IBM Dilithium keys,
IBM ML-DSA keys, IBM ML-KEM keys, and ML-DSA keys
(all wrapped with the CCA APKA master key).
.TP
\fBasym\fP
Old-format RSA keys (RSA-CRT, private key section X'08')
(wrapped with the CCA ASYM master key).
.TP
\fBsym\fP
DES, 2DES, and 3DES keys
(wrapped with the CCA SYM master key).
.RE
.IP "\fB-s\fP|\fB--slotid\fP \fISLOTID\fP" 5
The PKCS#11 slot number. Required.

.SH "OLD RSA KEY MIGRATION"
.IP "\fB-m oldrsakeys\fP" 5
Converts old RSA keys (RSA-CRT) to the new format (RSA-AESC) and extracts the
public key section only from key objects containing the full RSA key token.
.IP "\fB-s\fP|\fB--slotid\fP \fISLOTID\fP" 5
The PKCS#11 slot number. Required.

.SH "FILES"
.IP "@localstatedir@/lib/opencryptoki/ccatok/TOK_OBJ/OBJ.IDX"
Contains the current list of public and private token objects for the CCA token.
.IP "@localstatedir@/lib/opencryptoki/ccatok/MK_SO"
Contains the Security Officer (SO) master key, encrypted with the SO PIN.
Used by the \fBv2objectsv3\fP migration to verify the SO PIN and retrieve the
master key for re-encryption.
.IP "@localstatedir@/lib/opencryptoki/ccatok/MK_USER"
Contains the user master key, encrypted with the user PIN.
Used by the \fBv2objectsv3\fP migration to verify the user PIN.

.SH SEE ALSO
.PD 0
.TP
\fBREADME.cca_stdll\fP (in system's doc directory)
.PD
